      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body" start-indent="1in" end-indent="0pt">
         <fo:block id="service.resourcemonitoring">
            <fo:block font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
               <fo:block margin-left="0pt">
                  <fo:block font-size="24.8832pt" font-weight="bold">
                     <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                               xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                               keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                               space-before.optimum="0in"
                               space-before.minimum="0in"
                               space-before.maximum="0in"
                               hyphenate="false"
                               text-align="start"
                               start-indent="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                               font-size="28pt"
                               line-height="35pt"
                               font-weight="normal"
                               space-after="24pt">
                        <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                       provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                           <fo:list-item>
                              <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                 <fo:block>144</fo:block>
                              </fo:list-item-label>
                              <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                 <fo:block>Resource Monitoring Specification</fo:block>
                              </fo:list-item-body>
                           </fo:list-item>
                        </fo:list-block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                               xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                               font-family="ProductusOSGiBookcItalic"
                               font-size="18pt"
                               line-height="25pt">
                        <fo:basic-link internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring">
                           <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                      font-family="inherit"
                                      letter-spacing="inherit"
                                      hyphenate="inherit">Version 1.0</fo:inline>
                        </fo:basic-link>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e87">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Introduction</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.1</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Introduction</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Applications, executed on an OSGi platform, need hardware resources
    (CPU, memory, disk, storage space) and software resources (sockets,
    threads). As these resources are limited, applications have to share them
    in order to preserve system quality of service. This is a general fact in
    OSGi business cases where multiple bundles share the OSGi framework. This
    is especially the case when the framework is shared by distinct tenants,
    which are responsible for distinct set of bundles running with their own
    business logic and lifecycle.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The chapter defines an API for applications to monitor hardware
    resources consumed by any set of bundles. The bundle is the smallest unit
    that can be considered as a resource context, the entity that is
    monitored. Monitored data may enable applications to take decisions on
    management actions to apply. Resource management actions are mentioned as
    examples in this chapter, for example, actions on the lifecycle of
    components, bundles, the framework and the JVM, Java threads, raise of
    exceptions.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e91">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Essentials</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.2</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Essentials</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d296e93">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e94">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Monitoring</fo:inline> - Bundle execution
        resource usage is monitored.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e99">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Granular activation</fo:inline> - The resource
        monitoring service can be activated and deactivated per bundle or per
        bundle set.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e103">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Extensibility</fo:inline> - Five resource types are
        specified (CPU, memory, disk storage, alive thread and in-use
        sockets). The list of monitored resource types is extensible and
        query-able.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e107">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Eventing</fo:inline> - The resource monitoring service
        notifies interested entities of exceeded limits.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e111">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Entities</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.3</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Entities</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d296e113">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e114">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Resource Context</fo:inline> - A logical entity for
        resource accounting. A context may be related to a single bundle or a
        set of bundles.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e118">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">System Resource Context</fo:inline> - Resource context
        of the core framework.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e122">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Platform Resource Context</fo:inline> - A Resource
        context monitoring the resource usage of the platform as a
        whole.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e126">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Resource Monitor</fo:inline> - Monitors the usage of a
        specific resource type for a specific Resource Context. Resource
        Monitors track resource usage. They hold Resource Thresholds
        instances. Resource Monitor object implementation may depend on
        standard or proprietary JVM APIs, and on operating system
        features.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e130">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Resource Monitor Factory</fo:inline> - A factory
        creating Resource Monitor instances for every Resource Context.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e134">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">CPU Monitor</fo:inline> - Resource Monitor used to
        monitor CPU.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e138">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Memory Monitor</fo:inline> - Resource Monitor used to
        monitor memory.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e142">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Socket Monitor</fo:inline> - Resource Monitor used to
        monitor socket resource.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e146">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Disk Storage Monitor</fo:inline> - Resource Monitor for
        disk storage usage.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e150">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Thread Monitor</fo:inline> - Resource Monitor used to
        monitor alive Java Thread objects.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e154">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Resource Listener</fo:inline> - A Resource Listener
        receives resource threshold notifications.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e159">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Resource Event</fo:inline> - A Resource Event defines a
        notification to be synchronously sent to Resource Listener
        instances.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e163">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Resource Context Listener</fo:inline> - A Resource
        Context Listener receives notifications about resource context
        creation and configuration.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e167">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Resource Context Event</fo:inline> - A Resource Context
        Event defines a notification to be sent to Resource Context Listeners
        instances.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e171">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Resource Monitoring Service</fo:inline> - This is a
        singleton entity which manages Resource Context instances. It is used
        to create new Resource Context instances and to enumerate existing
        contexts.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e175">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Resource Monitoring Client</fo:inline> - Makes any
        decision to ensure the quality of the service of the system. They use
        the Resource Monitoring Service to create Resource Context instances.
        It configures them by adding bundles and Resource Monitors.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                      space-before.optimum="1em"
                      space-before.maximum="2em"
                      space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                      space-after.optimum="1em"
                      space-after.maximum="2em"
                      keep-together.within-column="always"
                      id="service.resourcemonitoring_bibliomixed_id_20141210_15h18_rfc_fig_2">
               <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                         xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                         space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt"
                         font-weight="normal"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                         space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                         space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                         start-indent="0pt"
                         font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-style="italic"
                         keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                  <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                 provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                     <fo:list-item>
                        <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                           <fo:block>Figure 144.1</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-label>
                        <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                           <fo:block>Resource monitoring class diagram specification.</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-body>
                     </fo:list-item>
                  </fo:list-block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block id="d296e181" text-align="center">
                  <fo:external-graphic src="url(file:///home/stbischof/git/OSGI_MIGRATE/osgi_target/org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring/spec/org.osgi.spec.service.resourcemonitoring/src/main/resources/spec/service.resourcemonitoring_resource_monitoring_specification_class_diagram_rev_01.svg)"
                                       width="auto"
                                       height="auto"
                                       content-width="5.000in"
                                       content-height="3.5in"
                                       text-align="center"/>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e184">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Operation Summary</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.4</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Operation Summary</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Resource Monitoring Clients use the Resource Monitoring Service
    service to create Resource Contexts. These clients set bundles or group of
    bundles to Resource Contexts. They also request every Resource Monitor
    Factory to create Resource Monitors for a resource type. These Resource
    Monitors are associated to a single Resource Context.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">When activated, Resource Monitors provide the current resource usage
    per Resource Context. Then, they check whether the current resource usage
    is compatible with the thresholds held by their associated Resource
    Listeners. When one of these thresholds is violated, the related Resource
    Monitor notifies the Resource Listener holding this threshold.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The Resource Monitoring Service manages the set of Resource
    Contexts. Resource Contexts are persistent between platform restarts.
    Resource Context Listeners are notified when a Resource Context is created
    or deleted or when a Resource Context configuration (that is, adding or
    removing of bundle) is updated.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e189">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Resource Context</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.5</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Resource Context</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContext">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ResourceContext</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> instance is a logical entity used to account
    resource usage. Every Resource Context defines a bundle scope which can be
    either a single bundle or a set of bundles. Once the bundle scope is
    defined, resources used by those bundles are monitored through a set of
    per-resource-type Resource Monitor instances.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Resource Context instances are persistent. The persistence of those
    instances is directly managed by the Resource Monitoring Service
    instance.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Each Resource Context is uniquely identified by a name. It can be
    retrieved through the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContext.getName--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">getName()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method. It can not be changed, that is it is
    definitively set when the Resource Context instance is created.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The Resource Context bundle scope is retrieved through the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContext.getBundleIds--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">getBundleIds()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method. This bundle scope can be extended through
    the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContext.addBundle-long-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">addBundle(long)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method. Bundles can also be removed from a
    Resource Context through the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContext.removeBundle-long-ResourceContext-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">removeBundle(long,ResourceContext)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method. For this last method, a Resource Context
    instance MAY be specified in order to associate the removed bundle to
    another Resource Context instance.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Resource Monitor instances are retrieved through <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContext.getMonitor-String-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">getMonitor(String)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method or the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContext.getMonitors--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">getMonitors()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method. The list of available resource types is
    retrieved through the Resource Monitoring Service singleton
    instance.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Resource Monitor instances are added to and removed from a Resource
    Context instance by calling either <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContext.addResourceMonitor-ResourceMonitor-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">addResourceMonitor(ResourceMonitor)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method or <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContext.removeResourceMonitor-ResourceMonitor-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">removeResourceMonitor(ResourceMonitor)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method. Both methods SHOULD only be called by
    <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitorFactory">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ResourceMonitorFactory</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> instances (see <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitorFactory.createResourceMonitor-ResourceContext-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">createResourceMonitor(ResourceContext)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method).</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A Resource Context is retrieved through the Resource Monitoring
    Service service.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A Resource Context instance can be deleted through <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContext.removeContext-ResourceContext-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">removeContext(ResourceContext)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method. The Resource Context input argument then
    defines a destination Resource Context instance for the bundles belonging
    to the to-be-removed Resource Context instance.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e229">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">System Resource Context</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.6</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>System Resource Context</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The System Resource Context is the Resource Context of the execution
    environment for the running OSGi bundles. It includes the resources of
    bundle "0". It is retrieved through the Resource Monitoring Service
    service.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The name of this context is “system”. See <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitoringService.SYSTEM_CONTEXT_NAME">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">SYSTEM_CONTEXT_NAME</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e236">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Framework Resource Context</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.7</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Framework Resource Context</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The Framework Resource Context is a Resource Context monitoring
    resources of the platform as a whole. It is retrieved through the Resource
    Monitoring Service service. This Resource Context holds all hosted bundles
    allowing access to the whole platform resource consumption.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The name of this context is “framework”. See <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitoringService.FRAMEWORK_CONTEXT_NAME">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">FRAMEWORK_CONTEXT_NAME</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e243">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Resource Monitor</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.8</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Resource Monitor</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitor">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ResourceMonitor</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> instance monitors a resource type consumed by the
    bundles of a specific Resource Context instance.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A Resource Context instance holds at most one Resource Monitor
    instance per monitor-able resource type. Resource Monitor instances are
    retrieved through their related Resource Context instance. Resource
    Monitor instances give access to their related Resource Context instance
    through a call to See <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitor.getContext--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">getContext()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The monitored resource type is retrieved through the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitor.getResourceType--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">getResourceType()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The current usage of a resource consumed by a Resource Context
    instance is given through the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitor.getUsage--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">getUsage()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method. This method returns a Java Object to be
    casted to the appropriate Java object type depending on the Resource type.
    The next table provides the expected Java Object type for each specified
    resource type:</fo:block>
            <fo:block xmlns:rx="http://www.renderx.com/XSL/Extensions"
                      space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                      space-before.optimum="1em"
                      space-before.maximum="2em"
                      space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                      space-after.optimum="1em"
                      space-after.maximum="2em"
                      keep-together.within-column="auto"
                      id="d296e261">
               <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                         xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                         space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt"
                         font-weight="normal"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                         space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                         space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                         start-indent="0pt"
                         font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-style="italic"
                         keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                  <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                 provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                     <fo:list-item>
                        <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                           <fo:block>Table 144.1</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-label>
                        <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                           <fo:block>Table of resource types.</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-body>
                     </fo:list-item>
                  </fo:list-block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:table border-before-width.conditionality="retain"
                         border-collapse="collapse"
                         table-layout="fixed"
                         width="100%">
                  <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="proportional-column-width(1)"/>
                  <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="proportional-column-width(1)"/>
                  <fo:table-column column-number="3" column-width="proportional-column-width(1)"/>
                  <fo:table-header start-indent="0pt" end-indent="0pt">
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always"
                                   keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                   font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt"
                                       text-align="left">
                           <fo:block>Type of Resource</fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt"
                                       text-align="left">
                           <fo:block>Expected Java Object type</fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt"
                                       text-align="left">
                           <fo:block>Value description</fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                  </fo:table-header>
                  <fo:table-footer start-indent="0pt" end-indent="0pt">
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always"
                                   keep-with-previous.within-column="always"
                                   font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt"
                                       text-align="left">
                           <fo:block>Disk storage space</fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt"
                                       text-align="left">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Long</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt"
                                       text-align="left">
                           <fo:block>Bytes on the bundle persistent storage area.</fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                  </fo:table-footer>
                  <fo:table-body start-indent="0pt" end-indent="0pt">
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt"
                                       text-align="left">
                           <fo:block>CPU</fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt"
                                       text-align="left">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Long</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt"
                                       text-align="left">
                           <fo:block>Cumulative CPU time in ns.</fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt"
                                       text-align="left">
                           <fo:block>Memory</fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt"
                                       text-align="left">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Long</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt"
                                       text-align="left">
                           <fo:block>Allocated memory in bytes.</fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt"
                                       text-align="left">
                           <fo:block>Threads</fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt"
                                       text-align="left">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Long</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt"
                                       text-align="left">
                           <fo:block>Number of alive thread.</fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt"
                                       text-align="left">
                           <fo:block>Socket</fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt"
                                       text-align="left">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Long</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt"
                                       text-align="left">
                           <fo:block>Number of in-use socket.</fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                  </fo:table-body>
               </fo:table>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">For example, for a <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.monitor.MemoryMonitor">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">MemoryMonitor</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> instance, a call to <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitor.getUsage--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">getUsage()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> returns a Long java object indicating the amount
    of memory the related Resource Context instance is consuming.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A Resource Monitor instance is enabled and disabled through <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitor.enable--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">enable()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> and <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitor.disable--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">disable()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> methods. The state (enabled or disabled) of a
    Resource Monitor is retrieved through a call to <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitor.isEnabled--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">isEnabled()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method. Enable and disable monitoring mechanisms
    on-the-fly on localized set of bundles may be crucial for performance
    issues. See <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="service.resourcemonitoring_bibliomixed_id_20150105_11h45_1">
                  <fo:inline color="inherit"
                             font-family="inherit"
                             letter-spacing="inherit"
                             hyphenate="inherit">[1] <fo:inline font-style="italic">Adaptive Monitoring of End-user OSGi based Home Boxes</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A Resource Monitor instance can also be deleted (<fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitor.delete--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">delete()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method). <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitor.isDeleted--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">isDeleted()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method returns true if the ResourceMonitor
    instance has been deleted.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Five types of Resource Monitor are specified:</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d296e322">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e323">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>CPU Monitor</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e325">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>Memory Monitor</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e327">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>Socket Monitor</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e329">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>Disk Storage Monitor</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e331">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>Thread Monitor</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The support of any Resource Monitor is optional. This list MAY be
    extended by the solution vendor. The list of the types that are supported
    on the OSGi platform can be computed by querying <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitorFactory">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ResourceMonitorFactory</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> services. Resource monitoring algorithms may vary
    with factories, see <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="service.resourcemonitoring_bibliomixed_id_20150105_11h46_2">
                  <fo:inline color="inherit"
                             font-family="inherit"
                             letter-spacing="inherit"
                             hyphenate="inherit">[2] <fo:inline font-style="italic">Memory Monitoring in a Multi-tenant OSGi Execution Environment</fo:inline>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>.
    They are out of the scope of this specification.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e340">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Resource Monitor Factory</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.9</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Resource Monitor Factory</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitorFactory">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ResourceMonitorFactory</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> is a service that provides Resource Monitor
    instances of a specific resource type (for example, <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.monitor.CPUMonitor">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">CPUMonitor</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>, <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.monitor.MemoryMonitor">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">MemoryMonitor</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>, etc.) for every Resource Context.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Every Resource Monitor Factory service is registered with the
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">org.osgi.resourcemonitoring.ResourceType</fo:inline> mandatory property,
    see <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitorFactory.RESOURCE_TYPE_PROPERTY">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">RESOURCE_TYPE_PROPERTY</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>. This property indicates which type of Resource
    Monitor a Resource Monitor Factory is able to create. The type can also be
    retrieved through a call to <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitorFactory.getType--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">getType()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>. The type MUST be unique (two Resource Monitor
    Factory services MUST not have the same type).</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">New Resource Monitor instances are created by a call to <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitorFactory.createResourceMonitor-ResourceContext-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">createResourceMonitor(ResourceContext)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>. This method returns a new Resource Monitor
    instance associated to the provided Resource Context instance. The
    ResourceMonitorFactory MUST call <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContext.addResourceMonitor-ResourceMonitor-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">addResourceMonitor(ResourceMonitor)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> to associate the newly created ResourceMonitor
    with the provided ResourceContext instance. The newly created Resource
    Monitor is disabled, that is, it is initially not monitoring the Resource
    Context resource consumption. It can be activated through a call to <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitor.enable--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">enable()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Resource Monitor instances are deleted by calling <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitor.delete--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">delete()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A Resource Monitor instance MUST only be created through its <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitorFactory">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ResourceMonitorFactory</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Resource Monitor Factory instances should be only used by the
    Resource Monitoring Service singleton instance. The Resource Monitoring
    Service singleton instance performs a service lookup on all existing
    Resource Monitor Factories. It uses a Resource Monitor Factory instance
    when it has to create a new Resource Context instance and their associated
    Resource Monitor instances.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e376">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">CPU Monitor</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.10</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>CPU Monitor</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.monitor.CPUMonitor">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">CPUMonitor</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> instance is a Resource Monitor used to monitor the
    CPU usage of the bundles belonging to a Resource Context.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">CPU usage and thresholds are expressed as a cumulative number of
    nanoseconds (long). The encapsulated value can be retrieved with the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.monitor.CPUMonitor.getCPUUsage--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">getCPUUsage()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">In case where a threshold is reached, the CPU Monitor instance
    generates an event triggering Resource Monitoring Clients defined
    corrective actions (for example, decrease thread priority).</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e387">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Memory Monitor</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.11</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Memory Monitor</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.monitor.MemoryMonitor">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">MemoryMonitor</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> instance monitors and limits the memory used by
    the bundles of a Resource Context instance.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Memory is accounted as bytes. Memory usage and thresholds are long
    java objects. The encapsulated value can be retrieved through the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.monitor.MemoryMonitor.getMemoryUsage--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">getMemoryUsage()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">When an error threshold is reached, the next memory allocation MAY
    be prevented by the system and MAY throw a specific Exception in the
    associated context.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e398">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Socket Monitor</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.12</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Socket Monitor</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.monitor.SocketMonitor">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">SocketMonitor</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> instance monitors and limits the number of
    existing sockets (for example, TCP, UDP) which are considered to be in use
    (for example, listening for incoming packet, bound, or sending outgoing
    packets).</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A Socket is considered to be in-use state when a native socket file
    descriptor is created. It leaves this state when this socket file
    descriptor is deleted.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The number of in-use sockets is a long. The encapsulated value can
    be retrieved using <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.monitor.SocketMonitor.getSocketUsage--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">getSocketUsage()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">When an <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.ERROR">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ERROR</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> threshold is reached, the next socket file
    descriptor creation in the associated context MAY throw a
    SocketException.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e413">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Disk Storage Monitor</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.13</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Disk Storage Monitor</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.monitor.DiskStorageMonitor">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">DiskStorageMonitor</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> instance monitors and limits the use of persistent
    storage within Bundle Persistent Storage Area a Resource Context (the
    bundles actually belonging to it) consumes.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Disk Storage is expressed as a number of bytes of type long. The
    encapsulated value can be retrieved using <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.monitor.DiskStorageMonitor.getUsedDiskStorage--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">getUsedDiskStorage()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">An IOException MAY be thrown in the associated context when an <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.ERROR">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ERROR</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> threshold is reached.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e427">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Thread Monitor</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.14</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Thread Monitor</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.monitor.ThreadMonitor">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ThreadMonitor</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> instance monitors and limits the number of alive
    Java Thread objects for a Resource Context instance. A Thread is
    considered to be alive when it is in the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">RUNNABLE</fo:inline>,
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">BLOCKED</fo:inline>, <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">WAITING</fo:inline> or <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">TIMED_WAITING</fo:inline>
    thread state.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Usage and thresholds are Java int objects. The encapsulated value
    can be retrieved using <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.monitor.ThreadMonitor.getAliveThreads--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">getAliveThreads()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">When an <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.ERROR">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ERROR</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> threshold is reached, any further thread
    activation will be prevented in the associated context. An InternalError
    exception MAY also be thrown in the associated context.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e449">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Resource Listener</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.15</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Resource Listener</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceListener">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ResourceListener</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> receives notifications about resource usage for a
    specific Resource Context and a specific type of resource. A notification
    will be sent to a Resource Listener when one of its thresholds is
    violated.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A Resource Listener holds two types of threshold:</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d296e456">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e457">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>A lower threshold type. This kind of threshold is reached when
        the monitored resource usage decreases below the threshold.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e459">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>An upper threshold type. An upper threshold is reached when the
        monitored resource usage exceeds this threshold.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Each of them have two levels:</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d296e462">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e463">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>a <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.WARNING">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">WARNING</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> level.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e468">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>an <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.ERROR">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">ERROR</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> level.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A threshold has the following state diagram, which transitions are
    associated to events:</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                      space-before.optimum="1em"
                      space-before.maximum="2em"
                      space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                      space-after.optimum="1em"
                      space-after.maximum="2em"
                      keep-together.within-column="always"
                      id="service.resourcemonitoring_bibliomixed_id_20141211_16h06_rfc_fig_3">
               <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                         xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                         space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt"
                         font-weight="normal"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                         space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                         space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                         start-indent="0pt"
                         font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-style="italic"
                         keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                  <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                 provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                     <fo:list-item>
                        <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                           <fo:block>Figure 144.2</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-label>
                        <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                           <fo:block>Threshold state diagram.</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-body>
                     </fo:list-item>
                  </fo:list-block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block id="d296e476" text-align="center">
                  <fo:external-graphic src="url(file:///home/stbischof/git/OSGI_MIGRATE/osgi_target/org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring/spec/org.osgi.spec.service.resourcemonitoring/src/main/resources/spec/ResourceThresholdState.svg)"
                                       width="auto"
                                       height="auto"
                                       content-width="auto"
                                       content-height="3.5in"
                                       text-align="center"/>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A threshold state depends on the current consumption of resource and
    the type of threshold (upper or lower threshold).</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A Resource Listener is registered as an OSGi service. The
    implementer must provide the two following mandatory properties:</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d296e481">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e482">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceListener.RESOURCE_CONTEXT">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">RESOURCE_CONTEXT</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> property – a String defining the name of
        Resource Context for which the Listener want to receive threshold
        notifications.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e486">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceListener.RESOURCE_TYPE">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">RESOURCE_TYPE</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> property – a String defining which type of
        resource the listener wants to monitor.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">It also has to provide at least one of these four properties when
    registered as an OSGi service:</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d296e492">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e493">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceListener.UPPER_WARNING_THRESHOLD">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">UPPER_WARNING_THRESHOLD</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e496">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceListener.UPPER_ERROR_THRESHOLD">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">UPPER_ERROR_THRESHOLD</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e499">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceListener.LOWER_WARNING_THRESHOLD">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">LOWER_WARNING_THRESHOLD</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e502">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceListener.LOWER_ERROR_THRESHOLD">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">LOWER_ERROR_THRESHOLD</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">These properties are mapped to the four types of threshold values a
    Resource Listener may support. The service properties are used to notify
    the associated Resource Monitor when one of these threshold values is
    modified.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Threshold values can also be retrieved through a set of getter
    methods. All of these methods returns a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Comparable</fo:inline> object
    used by the associated Resource Monitor in order to determine the current
    state of the current usage.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
               <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceListener.RESOURCE_CONTEXT">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">RESOURCE_CONTEXT</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> and <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceListener.RESOURCE_TYPE">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">RESOURCE_TYPE</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> properties are used by Resource Monitors to
    identify their associated Resource Listeners. Once associated, a Resource
    Monitor retrieves the threshold settings using service properties. When
    one of its thresholds is reached, the Resource Monitor calls <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceListener.notify-ResourceEvent-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">notify(ResourceEvent)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Two examples of resource consumption are explained below, first with
    in-use sockets monitoring, second with CPU monitoring. The next picture
    shows the state diagram of the number of in-use state socket over the
    time.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                      space-before.optimum="1em"
                      space-before.maximum="2em"
                      space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                      space-after.optimum="1em"
                      space-after.maximum="2em"
                      keep-together.within-column="always"
                      id="service.resourcemonitoring_bibliomixed_id_20141211_16h07_rfc_fig_4">
               <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                         xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                         space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt"
                         font-weight="normal"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                         space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                         space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                         start-indent="0pt"
                         font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-style="italic"
                         keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                  <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                 provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                     <fo:list-item>
                        <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                           <fo:block>Figure 144.3</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-label>
                        <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                           <fo:block>Number of in-use sockets over the time.</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-body>
                     </fo:list-item>
                  </fo:list-block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block id="d296e520" text-align="center">
                  <fo:external-graphic src="url(file:///home/stbischof/git/OSGI_MIGRATE/osgi_target/org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring/spec/org.osgi.spec.service.resourcemonitoring/src/main/resources/spec/LowerAndUpperThreshold.svg)"
                                       width="auto"
                                       height="auto"
                                       content-width="auto"
                                       content-height="3.5in"
                                       text-align="center"/>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">In our example, the lower warning threshold and the lower error
    threshold of the Resource Listener are respectively set to 10 and 5. When
    the number of in-use sockets decreases under 10, the usage goes from the
    <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.NORMAL">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">NORMAL</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> state to the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.WARNING">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">WARNING</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> state and the Resource Listener receives a <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.WARNING">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">WARNING</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> event. If the number of in-use state sockets
    decreases again and goes down to 5, the usage goes from the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.WARNING">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">WARNING</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> state to the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.ERROR">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ERROR</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> state and the Resource Listener receives a <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.ERROR">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ERROR</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> Resource Event.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The upper threshold is also set. The upper warning threshold and the
    upper error threshold are respectively set to 100 and 1000 in-use state
    sockets. When the number of sockets reaches 100, the usage goes from the
    <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.NORMAL">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">NORMAL</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> state to the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.WARNING">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">WARNING</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> state and the Resource Listener receives a <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.WARNING">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">WARNING</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> Resource Event. If this number is still increasing
    and exceeds 1000, then the usage goes from the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.WARNING">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">WARNING</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> state to the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.ERROR">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ERROR</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> state and the Resource Listener receives an <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.ERROR">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ERROR</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> Resource Event.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">This is a typical use case for a Java Web server. Indeed, one of the
    most important quality of service indicator is the number of in-use state
    sockets a java web server is handling. A low number of in-use state
    sockets may indicate the java web server encounters network problems. On
    the contrary, a high number of in-use state socket may be the result of an
    external network attack or it could also indicates the java web server is
    overused and its administrator should take actions to load-balance the
    charge to another java web server instance.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">For other resource types, only upper thresholds may be useful. The
    next diagram shows the CPU consumption a Resource Context is using over
    the time:</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                      space-before.optimum="1em"
                      space-before.maximum="2em"
                      space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                      space-after.optimum="1em"
                      space-after.maximum="2em"
                      keep-together.within-column="always"
                      id="service.resourcemonitoring_bibliomixed_id_20141211_16h08_rfc_fig_5">
               <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                         xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                         space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt"
                         font-weight="normal"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                         space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                         space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                         start-indent="0pt"
                         font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-style="italic"
                         keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                  <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                 provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                     <fo:list-item>
                        <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                           <fo:block>Figure 144.4</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-label>
                        <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                           <fo:block>CPU consumption (%) over the time – Upper Threshold.</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-body>
                     </fo:list-item>
                  </fo:list-block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block id="d296e558" text-align="center">
                  <fo:external-graphic src="url(file:///home/stbischof/git/OSGI_MIGRATE/osgi_target/org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring/spec/org.osgi.spec.service.resourcemonitoring/src/main/resources/spec/UpperThreshold.svg)"
                                       width="auto"
                                       height="auto"
                                       content-width="auto"
                                       content-height="3.5in"
                                       text-align="center"/>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">In this example, only the upper threshold is set. The upper warning
    threshold is set to 50%, the error one is set to 75%. CPU consumption
    fluctuates between 0 and 50%, the usage is in the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.NORMAL">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">NORMAL</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> state. Then it increases and reaches 50%. The
    usage then goes from the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.NORMAL">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">NORMAL</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> state to the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.WARNING">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">WARNING</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> state and the Resource Listener holding the
    threshold receives a <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.WARNING">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">WARNING</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> Resource Event.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Afterwards, CPU consumption decreases under 50%; the usage goes from
    the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.WARNING">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">WARNING</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> state to the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.NORMAL">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">NORMAL</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> state. The related Resource listener receives a
    <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.NORMAL">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">NORMAL</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> Resource Event.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">It then increases again and exceeds 50%. The usage goes to the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.WARNING">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">WARNING</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> state. CPU consumption is still increasing and
    exceeds 75%. At this moment, the usage goes from the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.WARNING">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">WARNING</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> state to the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.ERROR">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ERROR</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> state and the related Resource Listener receives
    an <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.ERROR">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ERROR</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> Resource Event.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">After some seconds in the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.ERROR">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ERROR</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> state, the Resource Listener implementation stops
    the bundle in order to preserve the quality of service.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The choice of the type of threshold (lower or upper, or both of
    them) depends on the type of resource and the needs of the Resource
    Monitoring Clients providing the Resource Listener. Other resources like
    the free memory may take advantage of a lower threshold.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e594">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Resource Event</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.16</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Resource Event</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ResourceEvent</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> instance is an event synchronously sent to a
    Resource Listener when one of its thresholds is reached. This event is
    notified to a Resource Listener through a call to
    ResourceListener.notify(ResourceEvent).</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A Resource Event has a type among the following ones:</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d296e601">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e602">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.ERROR">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">ERROR</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> – The resource consumption reaches either the
        upper or the lower error threshold of the Resource Listener receiving
        this event.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e606">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.WARNING">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">WARNING</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> – The resource consumption reaches either the
        upper or the lower warning threshold of the Resource Listener
        receiving this event.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e610">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.NORMAL">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">NORMAL</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> – The resource consumption is back from
        warning or error state to normal state.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The Resource Listener instance analyzes this event by calling the
    following methods:</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d296e615">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e616">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.getValue--">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">getValue()</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> method returns the resource consumption at the
        time when the Resource Event instance was generated.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e620">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.isUpperThreshold--">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">isUpperThreshold()</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> method returns true if the reached threshold
        is an upper threshold type. If this method returns false, this is a
        lower threshold.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e624">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.getType--">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">getType()</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> method indicates the state (WARNING, ERROR, or
        NORMAL) of the resource usage.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e628">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent.getContext--">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">getContext()</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> method returns the Resource Context instance
        related to this event. The Resource Listener can use it to retrieve
        the Resource Monitor instance. For example,
        <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">event.getContext().getMonitor(event.getResourceType())</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e634">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Resource Context Listener</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.17</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Resource Context Listener</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContextListener">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ResourceContextListener</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> instance receives notifications about Resource
    Context lifecycle and configuration.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A notification will be sent when:</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d296e641">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e642">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>A Resource Context is created.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e644">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>A Resource Context is updated, that is, a bundle has been added
        or removed from a Resource Context instance.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e646">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>A Resource Context is deleted.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">An application which is interested in notifications has to register
    a Resource Context Listener instance as an OSGi service. The application
    may provide a set of properties at registration time to reduce the number
    of notifications a Resource Listener instance will receive. The available
    property is:</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d296e649">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e650">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContextListener.RESOURCE_CONTEXT">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">RESOURCE_CONTEXT</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> property – An array of String defining the
        name of Resource Context instances. If defined, a Resource Listener
        instance will only receive notifications related to these specified
        Resource Context instances.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A Resource Context Listener instance is notified through a call to
    <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContextListener.notify-ResourceContextEvent-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">notify(ResourceContextEvent)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e658">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Resource Context Event</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.18</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Resource Context Event</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContextEvent">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ResourceContextEvent</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> instance is an event sent to Resource Context
    Listener instances through a call to the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContextListener.notify-ResourceContextEvent-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">notify(ResourceContextEvent)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A Resource Context Event has a type among the four following
    ones:</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d296e667">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e668">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContextEvent.RESOURCE_CONTEXT_CREATED">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">RESOURCE_CONTEXT_CREATED</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> – A new Resource Context instance has been
        created.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e672">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContextEvent.RESOURCE_CONTEXT_REMOVED">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">RESOURCE_CONTEXT_REMOVED</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> – A Resource Context instance has been
        deleted.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e676">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContextEvent.BUNDLE_ADDED">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">BUNDLE_ADDED</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> – A bundle has been added in the scope of a
        Resource Context instance.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e680">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContextEvent.BUNDLE_REMOVED">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">BUNDLE_REMOVED</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> – A bundle has been removed from the scope of
        a Resource Context instance.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">In the case of a <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContextEvent.RESOURCE_CONTEXT_CREATED">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">RESOURCE_CONTEXT_CREATED</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> event or a <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContextEvent.RESOURCE_CONTEXT_REMOVED">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">RESOURCE_CONTEXT_REMOVED</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> event, a call to <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContextEvent.getContext--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">getContext()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> returns the targeted Resource Context
    instance.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">In the case of a <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContextEvent.BUNDLE_ADDED">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">BUNDLE_ADDED</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> type or <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContextEvent.BUNDLE_REMOVED">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">BUNDLE_REMOVED</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> type, <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContextEvent.getBundleId--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">getBundleId()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> returns the id of the bundle to be added to or
    removed from. The related Resource Context instance is given by a call to
    <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContextEvent.getContext--">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">getContext()</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e702">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Resource Monitoring Service</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.19</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Resource Monitoring Service</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitoringService">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">ResourceMonitoringService</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> manages the Resource Context instances. The
    Resource Monitoring Service is available through the OSGi service
    registry.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">This service holds the existing Resource Context instances. Resource
    Context instances are created by calling the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitoringService.createContext-String-ResourceContext-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">createContext(String,ResourceContext)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method. The caller provides a context name as a
    string and optionally a template as a ResourceContext object.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The list of existing Resource Context instances can be retrieved
    through the following methods:</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d296e713">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e714">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitoringService.getContext-String-">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">getContext(String)</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> – returns the ResourceContext with the
        specified resource context name.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e718">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitoringService.getContext-long-">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">getContext(long)</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> – returns the ResourceContext associated to
        the provided bundle id.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e722">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitoringService.listContext--">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">listContext()</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> – retrieve all existing Resource Context
        instances as an array.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The Resource Monitoring Service singleton manages the persistence of
    the Resource Context instances. The following properties are
    stored:</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d296e727">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e728">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>name of the Resource Context.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e730">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>list of the bundles belonging to the Resource Context.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e732">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>list of the Resource Monitor instances. For each one: the
        sampling period, and the monitoring period.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The way the Resource Monitoring Service persists the Resource
    Context instances is implementation specific. The implementer is free to
    use any file format and file location it wants. At startup, the Resource
    Monitoring Service will load the persisted Resource Context instances to
    restore the state prior to shutdown.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e735">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Resource Monitoring Client</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.20</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Resource Monitoring Client</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A Resource Monitoring Client uses the Resource Monitoring Service
    singleton instance to apply Resource Monitoring policies. These entities
    MAY:</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d296e738">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e739">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>create and configure Resource Context instances (resource
        thresholds, bundle scope)</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d296e741">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>take any decisions (stop a bundle, uninstall a bundle) if a
        Resource Context exceeds resource limit.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">These policies are out of the scope of this specification.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d296e745">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Security</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.21</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Security</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">It is recommended that
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">ServicePermission[ResourceMonitoringService|ResourceMonitoringFactory|ResourceListener,
    REGISTER|GET]</fo:inline> be used sparingly and only for bundles that are
    trusted.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>144.22</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring<fo:inline id="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring-version"/>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"/>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
Resource Monitoring Package Version 1.0.

 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 Bundles wishing to use this package must list the package in the
 Import-Package header of the bundle's manifest. This package has two types of
 users: the consumers that use the API in this package and the providers that
 implement the API in this package.

 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 Example import for consumers using the API in this package:
 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 {@code  Import-Package: org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring; version="[1.0,2.0)"}
 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 Example import for providers implementing the API in this package:
 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 {@code  Import-Package: org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring; version="[1.0,1.1)"}</fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d296e764">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>144.22.1</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Summary</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d296e766">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d296e767">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContext">
                                 <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                            font-family="inherit"
                                            letter-spacing="inherit"
                                            hyphenate="inherit">
                                    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                               font-size="9pt"
                                               letter-spacing="0.08em">ResourceContext</fo:inline>
                                 </fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> - 
Logical entity for resource accounting.
   </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d296e775">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContextEvent">
                                 <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                            font-family="inherit"
                                            letter-spacing="inherit"
                                            hyphenate="inherit">
                                    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                               font-size="9pt"
                                               letter-spacing="0.08em">ResourceContextEvent</fo:inline>
                                 </fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> - 
A Resource Context Event instance is an event sent to Resource Context
 Listener instances through a call to
 {@link ResourceContextListener#notify(ResourceContextEvent)} method.
   </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d296e783">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContextException">
                                 <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                            font-family="inherit"
                                            letter-spacing="inherit"
                                            hyphenate="inherit">
                                    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                               font-size="9pt"
                                               letter-spacing="0.08em">ResourceContextException</fo:inline>
                                 </fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> - 
Resource Context Exception.
   </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d296e791">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContextListener">
                                 <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                            font-family="inherit"
                                            letter-spacing="inherit"
                                            hyphenate="inherit">
                                    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                               font-size="9pt"
                                               letter-spacing="0.08em">ResourceContextListener</fo:inline>
                                 </fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> - 
 A <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">ResourceContextListener</fo:inline> is notified whenever:
 <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                                             provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                                             id="d296e801">
                                 <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                               space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                               space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                               id="d296e802">
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:block>a {@link ResourceContext} is created or deleted.</fo:block>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                                 <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                               space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                               space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                               id="d296e804">
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:block>a bundle is added or removed from a {@link ResourceContext}.</fo:block>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d296e807">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceEvent">
                                 <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                            font-family="inherit"
                                            letter-spacing="inherit"
                                            hyphenate="inherit">
                                    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                               font-size="9pt"
                                               letter-spacing="0.08em">ResourceEvent</fo:inline>
                                 </fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> - 
 An event is sent to a {@link ResourceListener} when resource usage violates
 one of their thresholds.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d296e815">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceListener">
                                 <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                            font-family="inherit"
                                            letter-spacing="inherit"
                                            hyphenate="inherit">
                                    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                               font-size="9pt"
                                               letter-spacing="0.08em">ResourceListener</fo:inline>
                                 </fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> - 
 A ResourceListener is an OSGi service which is notified when a Resource
 Context violates one of the threshold defined by the listener.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d296e823">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitor">
                                 <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                            font-family="inherit"
                                            letter-spacing="inherit"
                                            hyphenate="inherit">
                                    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                               font-size="9pt"
                                               letter-spacing="0.08em">ResourceMonitor</fo:inline>
                                 </fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> - 
Representation of the state of a resource for a resource context.
   </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d296e831">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitorException">
                                 <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                            font-family="inherit"
                                            letter-spacing="inherit"
                                            hyphenate="inherit">
                                    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                               font-size="9pt"
                                               letter-spacing="0.08em">ResourceMonitorException</fo:inline>
                                 </fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> - 
Resource Monitor Exception reports an invalid usage of a monitor.
   </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d296e839">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitorFactory">
                                 <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                            font-family="inherit"
                                            letter-spacing="inherit"
                                            hyphenate="inherit">
                                    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                               font-size="9pt"
                                               letter-spacing="0.08em">ResourceMonitorFactory</fo:inline>
                                 </fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> - 
A Resource Monitor Factory is a service that provides Resource Monitor
 instances of a specific resource type (for example, CPUMonitor, MemoryMonitor...)
 for every Resource Context.
   </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d296e847">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceMonitoringService">
                                 <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                            font-family="inherit"
                                            letter-spacing="inherit"
                                            hyphenate="inherit">
                                    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                               font-size="9pt"
                                               letter-spacing="0.08em">ResourceMonitoringService</fo:inline>
                                 </fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> - 
It manages the Resource Context instances.
   </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContext">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>144.22.2</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>public abstract ResourceContext</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">
Logical entity for resource accounting. A resource context has a group of
 member bundles, and a bundle can be a member of 0 or 1 resource context.
 
 </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">
 Resource Monitoring Clients can use the
 {@link ResourceMonitoringService#createContext(String, ResourceContext)}
 method to create ResourceContext instances.
 
 </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">
 Resource Monitoring Clients can use the {@link #getMonitor(String)} method to
 get {@link ResourceMonitor} instances for the supported resource types. These
 instances can then be used to monitor the usage of the resources, or the set
 usage limits.
 
 </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">
 ResourceContexts are retrieved through the {@link ResourceMonitoringService}
 OSGi service.</fo:block>
               <fo:block id="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContext.addBundle-long-">
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                                  margin-left="0pt"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                           <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                              <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                        xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                        font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                        font-weight="normal"
                                        keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                        space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                        space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                        space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                        text-align="start"
                                        start-indent="0pt"
                                        hyphenate="false">
                                 <fo:block font-size="9pt"
                                           line-height="11pt"
                                           space-before="5pt"
                                           space-after="5pt">
                                    <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                   provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                       <fo:list-item>
                                          <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                             <fo:block>144.22.2.1</fo:block>
                                          </fo:list-item-label>
                                          <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                             <fo:block>public abstract void addBundle(long bundleId) throws ResourceContextException</fo:block>
                                          </fo:list-item-body>
                                       </fo:list-item>
                                    </fo:list-block>
                                 </fo:block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                            xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                            space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt"
                            start-indent="0pt"
                            relative-align="baseline">
                     <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                    provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                        <fo:list-item>
                           <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                              <fo:block text-align="end" font-style="italic">
                                 <fo:block>bundleId</fo:block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-label>
                           <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                              <fo:block>The bundle to add to this resource context</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-body>
                        </fo:list-item>
                     </fo:list-block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                            xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                            space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt"
                            start-indent="0pt"
                            relative-align="baseline">
                     <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                    provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                        <fo:list-item>
                           <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                              <fo:block text-align="end" font-style="italic">
                                 <fo:inline font-weight="normal"
                                            font-style="normal"
                                            baseline-shift="-1pt"
                                            font-size="9pt">□</fo:inline>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-label>
                           <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                              <fo:block>
Adds a bundle to the resource context. The bundle will be a member of the
 context until it is uninstalled, or explicitly removed from the context
 with {@link #removeBundle(long)} method or
 {@link #removeBundle(long, ResourceContext)} method.
 </fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-body>
                        </fo:list-item>
                     </fo:list-block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt">
 Resources previously allocated by this bundle (in another resource
 context) will not be moved to this resource context. The change applies
 only for future allocations.
 </fo:block>
                  <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt">
 A {@link ResourceContextEvent} with type
 {@link ResourceContextEvent#BUNDLE_ADDED} will be sent.</fo:block>
                  <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                            xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                            space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt"
                            start-indent="0pt"
                            relative-align="baseline">
                     <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                    provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                        <fo:list-item>
                           <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                              <fo:block text-align="end" font-style="italic">
                                 <fo:block>Throws</fo:block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-label>
                           <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">ResourceContextException</fo:inline>– For example, when the bundle can't be
         added to the ResourceContext.</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-body>
                        </fo:list-item>
                     </fo:list-block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block id="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContext.addResourceMonitor-ResourceMonitor-">
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                                  margin-left="0pt"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                           <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                              <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                        xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                        font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                        font-weight="normal"
                                        keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                        space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                        space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                        space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                        text-align="start"
                                        start-indent="0pt"
                                        hyphenate="false">
                                 <fo:block font-size="9pt"
                                           line-height="11pt"
                                           space-before="5pt"
                                           space-after="5pt">
                                    <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                   provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                       <fo:list-item>
                                          <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                             <fo:block>144.22.2.2</fo:block>
                                          </fo:list-item-label>
                                          <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                             <fo:block>public abstract void addResourceMonitor(ResourceMonitor&lt;?&gt; resourceMonitor) throws ResourceContextException</fo:block>
                                          </fo:list-item-body>
                                       </fo:list-item>
                                    </fo:list-block>
                                 </fo:block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                            xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                            space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt"
                            start-indent="0pt"
                            relative-align="baseline">
                     <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                    provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                        <fo:list-item>
                           <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                              <fo:block text-align="end" font-style="italic">
                                 <fo:block>resourceMonitor</fo:block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-label>
                           <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                              <fo:block>resourceMonitor instance to be added</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-body>
                        </fo:list-item>
                     </fo:list-block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                            xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                            space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt"
                            start-indent="0pt"
                            relative-align="baseline">
                     <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                    provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                        <fo:list-item>
                           <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                              <fo:block text-align="end" font-style="italic">
                                 <fo:inline font-weight="normal"
                                            font-style="normal"
                                            baseline-shift="-1pt"
                                            font-size="9pt">□</fo:inline>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-label>
                           <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                              <fo:block>
Adds a new ResourceMonitor instance monitoring resource for this resource
 context. This method should be called only by ResourceMonitorFactory
 instance.
   </fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-body>
                        </fo:list-item>
                     </fo:list-block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                            xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                            space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt"
                            start-indent="0pt"
                            relative-align="baseline">
                     <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                    provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                        <fo:list-item>
                           <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                              <fo:block text-align="end" font-style="italic">
                                 <fo:block>Throws</fo:block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-label>
                           <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                              <fo:block>
                                 <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">ResourceContextException</fo:inline>– For example, when the monitor can't be
         added to the ResourceContext.</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-body>
                        </fo:list-item>
                     </fo:list-block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block id="org.osgi.service.resourcemonitoring.ResourceContext.equals-Object-">
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                                  margin-left="0pt"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                           <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                              <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                        xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                        font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                        font-weight="normal"
                                        keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                        space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                        space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                        space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                        text-align="start"
                                        start-indent="0pt"
                                        hyphenate="false">
                                 <fo:block font-size="9pt"
                                           line-height="11pt"
                                           space-before="5pt"
                                           space-after="5pt">
                                    <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                   provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                       <fo:list-item>
                                          <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                             <fo:block>144.22.2.3</fo:block>
                                          </fo:list-item-label>
                                          <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                             <fo:block>public abstract boolean equals(Object resourceContext)</fo:block>
                                          </fo:list-item-body>
                                       </fo:list-item>
                                    </fo:list-block>
                                 </fo:block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                            xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                            space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt"
                            start-indent="0pt"
                            relative-align="baseline">
                     <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                    provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                        <fo:list-item>
                           <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                              <fo:block text-align="end" font-style="italic">
                                 <fo:block>resourceContext</fo:block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-label>
                           <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
